<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Required by BOTH halves of the Wi-Fi scan, and by nothing else in the
	     app. Since iOS 14 an app may not send to, or receive from, a multicast
	     or broadcast address over a raw socket without this entitlement.

	     The exemption people usually remember does not apply here. Apple
	     exempts mDNS performed through the Bonjour APIs (NWBrowser, the old
	     NetService) because mDNSResponder does the multicast on the app's
	     behalf, and NSBonjourServices in Info.plist is what declares the
	     service types for that path. lib/services/real_network_scan_service.dart
	     uses neither: `multicast_dns` binds UDP 5353 and joins 224.0.0.251
	     itself, and the SSDP half sends M-SEARCH to 239.255.255.250 from its
	     own RawDatagramSocket. Both are raw multicast and both need this key.

	     Unlike a missing usage-description string, the failure is silent: the
	     sockets bind, the queries go out, nothing answers. That is
	     indistinguishable from an empty network from inside the app, and it is
	     what scanFailureFor() reports as LocalNetworkDeniedException, sending
	     the user to a Settings toggle that was never the problem.

	     Apple gates this entitlement behind a manual approval request; it
	     cannot simply be enabled in the App ID like most capabilities. See
	     docs/ios-from-linux.md for what to file and what breaks until it is
	     granted. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.multicast</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
